        "Title": "Learn Russian With Me! - #2",
        "Location": "LOCATION_OPULENT_STINGRAY",
        "PublicId": "126641958506",
        "ScenePath": "assembly:/_pro/scenes/missions/Opulent/mission_stingray/scene_stingray_basic.entity",
        "TileImage": "$($repository 413873f0-a573-4836-bc3f-46659344da71).Image",
        "Description": "Privyet agent, today&apos;s word is machete. The way you say it in Russian is мачете (pronounced &quot;mah-chye-te&quot;). Sorry it has to be on Haven Island. Good luck and have fun comrade!\r\rFun Fact: There is no &quot;h&quot; sound in Russian, which means that most things get written with a &quot;g&quot;. So Haven Island is said as Gaven Island. That almost sounds like Gay Men Island, which I think fits.",
